OL,3,GNEWSAClubs backing charity's CPR
OL,4,Achallenge
OL,5,
OL,6,FReading and Wycombe Wanderers are
OL,7,Fbacking a charity's lifesaving 24-hour
OL,8,Fchallenge and calling on their fans and
OL,9,Fbusinesses to take part.
OL,11,FThey are supporting the South Central
OL,12,FAmbulance Service's charity CPR-A-THON
OL,13,Fwhich will be held at their respective
OL,14,Fgrounds days before their League One
OL,15,Fmatch later this month.
OL,17,FThe charity wants teams of up to 10
OL,18,Fpeople to take turns performing 30
OL,19,Fchest compressions on a CPR manikin
OL,20,Fbefore handing over to a team member,
OL,21,Fwith them continuing their efforts for
OL,22,F24 hours.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
